@startuml phase2-4-ada-ecu-admission
' R13 track admission state machine - PlantUML form of
' documents/Requirements/vehicleC_track_admission_state_machine.png, made unambiguous for implementation.
' One machine, both sources (own_sensor and v2x_relayed); see ada-ecu-design-decisions.md D3,
' cited from ada-ecu-hld.md section 6.

title R13 admission state machine - one machine, both perception sources

state "not_tracked" as NT : absent from the store\n(no entry, not an entry with state=not_tracked)
state "tentative" as TE : in the store, confirming\nhits counter 1..CONFIRM_HITS-1
state "tracked" as TR : in the store, published to the CRA

[*] --> NT

NT --> TE : update with distance <= GATE_ENTER_M\n(create entry, hits = 1)
TE --> TE : update with distance <= GATE_ENTER_M\n(hits += 1)
TE --> TR : hits >= CONFIRM_HITS
TR --> TR : update with distance <= GATE_EXIT_M\n(refresh lastUpdated)

TE --> NT : update with distance > GATE_ENTER_M\n(lost / out of range - erase, hits = 0)
TE --> NT : now - lastUpdated > TRACK_TIMEOUT_MS\n(messages stopped - erase, hits = 0)
TR --> NT : update with distance > GATE_EXIT_M\n(hysteresis drop - erase, hits = 0)
TR --> NT : now - lastUpdated > TRACK_TIMEOUT_MS\n(messages stopped - erase, hits = 0)

note right of NT
  Definitions (HLD D3):
  * update = one admission-relevant observation for a track id:
      v2x_relayed -> one R2 message (object.distance)
      own_sensor  -> one detector JSONL line (distance)
  * GATE_ENTER_M (30 m) admits and holds while tentative;
    GATE_EXIT_M (35 m) holds only once tracked - the hysteresis band.
  * TRACK_TIMEOUT_MS is a timeout, not a message count:
    the two sources run at independently configured cadences,
    and "messages stopped" cannot be counted from messages that never arrive.
    It is measured on CLOCK_MONOTONIC, against the per-track stamp the store
    keeps beside `lastUpdated` (design decision D10), so a host clock step
    cannot expire every track at once.
  * The store is the sole writer of `state`; the `state` field on
    incoming detector / R2-derived objects is ignored.
  * Every edge writes one track_transition event to the R18 [EVT] stream.
end note

@enduml
